attempts: 0
body: "Shepherd ironhorse test262 ratchet head #1599 to passing CI on its own, ready to be consolidated into llm. The maintainer: \"merge the various heads of the ratchet first, provided they are individually shepherded to passing in CI and ready to be consolidated.\"\n\nProject: endojs/endo-but-for-bots. PR #1599, \"fix(ironhorse-vm): wrap sync iterators in an AsyncFromSyncIterator\", branch ironhorse-test262-ratchet-async-from-sync-20261101, base llm.\n\nBefore this job was released, llm gained the XS oracle's pinned Math (job ironhorse-xs-oracle-pinned-libm); before that, every head was red only on test-ironhorse-oracle and ironhorse-oracle-sanitizers, for that reason and no other.\n\n1. Merge current llm into the head (the repo merges PRs by rebase; a merge of llm into the head is fine for shepherding, and a rebase is fine if it is clean).\n2. Resolve conflicts. Generated files are regenerated, never hand-merged: snapshot goldens with the ignored test regenerate_persistence_identities in rust/engine/ironhorse-snapshot/tests/state_golden.rs; whole-tree expectations with rust/engine/ironhorse-262/scripts/expectation-shards.sh; fuzz seeds as their test documents.\n3. Run what CI runs for this head's changed crates, including the oracle lane (rust/engine: cargo test --locked -p ironhorse-compile -p ironhorse-regexp -p ironhorse-262 -p ironhorse-fuzz --features ironhorse-compile/parity,ironhorse-regexp/parity, RUST_MIN_STACK=33554432), and cargo clippy -D warnings. Fix what fails within the head's purpose. The floor only rises: a covered case lost is a failure to fix, not a baseline to rewrite.\n4. Commit on the head's branch. Report: what changed, tests run and their results, the covered-count delta against llm, and any file another ratchet head also changes (consolidation will need it). You have no remote: the steward pushes the branch and watches CI."
